{"name":"Millennial Grey","hex":"#7b7b7d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"millennial grey","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth standard form of millennial gray."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard form of millennial gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/millennial_grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Millennial grey","blocks":[{"text":"Millennial grey is a pejorative name given to a desaturated colour scheme in interior design, which some media commentators have claimed appeals to the sensibilities of the millennial generation in the early 21st century, but which has also been criticised as a fabrication by marketers, similar to other claimed intergenerational divides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/EFTA00002084_-_Modern_kitchen_with_gray_wood_floors_stainless_steel_appliances_and_large_windows_leading_to_a_balcony.jpg/330px-EFTA00002084_-_Modern_kitchen_with_gray_wood_floors_stainless_steel_appliances_and_large_windows_leading_to_a_balcony.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennial_grey","wikidata":"Q139750658"},{"title":"Millennials","blocks":[{"text":"Millennials, also known as Generation Y or Gen Y, are the demographic cohort following Generation X and preceding Generation Z. Researchers and popular media use the early 1980s as starting birth years and the mid-1990s to early 2000s as ending birth years, with the generation typically being defined as people born from 1981 to 1996. Most millennials are the children of baby boomers and older Gen Xers, and are often the parents of younger Generation Z and Generation Alpha."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Generation_timeline_simple.svg/330px-Generation_timeline_simple.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennials","wikidata":"Q277633"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/500px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/1280px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg/500px-Linkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Linkin Park was a popular music group among millennials[119]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALinkin_Park_-_Summer_Sonic_2006.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg/500px-Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg/1280px-Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg/500px-Future_Music_Festival_2011_%285520592096%29.jpg?utm_s